    "result_text": "Patrons now carry shares, and backing is weighted by them. All 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\n**The change** (in `src/main/frontend/src/app/features/people/people.ts`):\n- **Shares:** 100.00 is split equally among a person's patrons in the order they were named. Each share is rounded half to even to two decimals, and whatever is left over goes to the first-named patron. Three patrons get 33.34, 33.33 and 33.33.\n- **Patrons cell:** shows `<name> <share>`, sorted by name and separated by comma and space, e.g. `Ben 33.34, Cam 33.33, Dot 33.33`.\n- **Backing:** for each patron, their settled figure over the last 90 days times their share \u00f7 100. Each patron's part is rounded half to even, then the parts are added up.\n\nShares come from the order patrons were added, which is already stored, so no database or API change was needed.\n\n**One decision for you:** the request can be read as rounding each patron's part or only the final sum. I round each part, the way the app already rounds percentages. The test data gives the same result either way, so the tests don't settle it. Switching to rounding only the sum is a small change if that's what you meant.\n\n**A second fix I made:** the test called \"patron shares scenario 1\" failed every time for a reason unrelated to this change. With an \"as of\" date set, re-loading a sheet failed if anyone on it had been merged away after a period closed. The code that rebuilds the sheet as of a date (`SheetHistory`) found a period's stored totals through the person they name, so the merged-away person's row was left behind and blocked the period from being cleared. It now finds those rows through their period. This is the only table it affects.",
